From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:56:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 122/167] hjviewer: Settings -> Security lists the connections
 this PC let in (TV-W9 Dart)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W9 (design w7-w9 3-3 and 5-4, D-16, critic 2-5): an installed Windows PC of an account build
gets the card '들어온 연결' / 'Incoming connections' in Settings -> Security, inside the
security settings' unlock (the card sits in the locked column, [목록 보기] greyed and blocked
until the administrator check or the unlock PIN). [목록 보기] opens '이 PC에 들어온 연결' (the
wide dialog frame, [새로 고침] and [닫기], back closes it), read with
main_get_common("hjv-incoming") when it opens and on [새로 고침] only. Rows newest first under
오늘 / 어제 / the date; per row the times, length and kind, the name and the spaced ID, and the
mark in the connection window's words (shield for same-account and staff; a staff row shows no
name, S-05; an unknown mark is never drawn as verified), how it got in, how it ended and the
reconnects. {"error":"ipc"} or a broken answer says the list could not be read; "on":false says
only an installed PC records. Names and IDs are cleaned of control and bidi characters again
before they are drawn. A screen reader hears each row as one sentence.
hjviewer_incoming_rules.dart holds the parsing and all texts (pure Dart, tested by
hjviewer_incoming_test.dart); hjviewer_incoming.dart draws them; desktop_setting_page.dart gets
the import and one card in the security tab.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
